/**
 * @mainpage Developer Guide 
 * 
 * @section dev_guide_summary Summary
 *
 * This developer guide is intended for users who seek to implement the Lime Suite NG library into custom applications or want to contribute to the development and
 * distribution of Lime Suite NG and its software components. 
 * 
 * Developers that seek to implement Lime Suite NG into custom applications are recommended to review the ``Introduction`` and ``Library`` pages.
 * ``Introduction`` page provides diagrams, which provide information about the communication flow of Lime Suite NG library. ``Library`` page provides 
 * reference to the library API, development guide for beginner and experienced developers as well as other important development information.
 * 
 * Developers that seek to contribute to the development and distribution of Lime Suite NG are recommended to review the ``Tools`` and ``Distribution`` pages. ``Tools`` page 
 * provides information about various development tools that can be used to increase efficiency of Lime Suite NG development process. ``Distribution`` page provides information 
 * about packaging and distribution of Lime Suite NG and its software components.
 * 
 * GUI tool page is intended for engineers who seek to use a Lime Suite NG provided advanced software tool for advanced LimeSDR device configurations.
 * 
 * ``LMS API (Legacy)`` page provides a limited support for legacy software. It is recommend to use the new Lime Suite NG library and its API. Some LMS API to Lime Suite NG API 
 * porting guidelines are provided in the ``Library`` page.
 * 
 * Topics of interest:
 * <ol>
 *     <li> @ref diagrams_intro </li>
 *     <li> @ref limesuiteng_api_ref_top "Library" </li>
 *     <li> @ref dev_tools_index "Tools" </li>
 *     <li> @ref software_distribution </li>
 *     <li> @ref gui_tool_index </li>
 *     <li> @ref lms_api_index </li>
 * </ol>
 * 
 */